From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz Sobala <lsobala1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 00:47:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: add Zicsr and Zifencei extensions to -march

binutils 2.38 switched to ISA spec 20191213, which moved the CSR instructions
into Zicsr and fence.i into Zifencei. U-Boot 2021.10 predates that, so with
any modern toolchain the RISC-V build dies before it gets anywhere:

  arch/riscv/cpu/start.S:67: Error: unrecognized opcode `csrw stvec,t0',
      extension `zicsr' required
  arch/riscv/lib/cache.c:12: Error: unrecognized opcode `fence.i',
      extension `zifencei' required

This is upstream's fix, with one deviation: the probe also passes -mabi.
cc-option-yn does not include the ABI flag, and Debian's riscv64 gcc defaults
to lp64d, so the bare probe fails with

  cc1: error: requested ABI requires '-march' to subsume the 'D' extension

which is about the ABI, not about Zicsr/Zifencei - and silently answering "n"
leaves the build broken in exactly the way this patch exists to fix. Passing
-mabi=$(ABI) makes the probe test what it means to test.

Only touches arch/riscv, so the ARM side of this family is unaffected.
---
diff --git a/arch/riscv/Makefile b/arch/riscv/Makefile
index 0b80eb8..fe60f69 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/Makefile
+++ b/arch/riscv/Makefile
@@ -24,7 +24,14 @@ ifeq ($(CONFIG_CMODEL_MEDANY),y)
 	CMODEL = medany
 endif
 
-ARCH_FLAGS = -march=$(ARCH_BASE)$(ARCH_A)$(ARCH_C) -mabi=$(ABI) \
+# Newer binutils versions default to ISA spec version 20191213 which moves some
+# instructions from the I extension to the Zicsr and Zifencei extensions.
+toolchain-need-zicsr-zifencei := $(call cc-option-yn, -mabi=$(ABI) -march=$(ARCH_BASE)$(ARCH_A)$(ARCH_C)_zicsr_zifencei)
+ifeq ($(toolchain-need-zicsr-zifencei),y)
+	ARCH_ZICSR_ZIFENCEI = _zicsr_zifencei
+endif
+
+ARCH_FLAGS = -march=$(ARCH_BASE)$(ARCH_A)$(ARCH_C)$(ARCH_ZICSR_ZIFENCEI) -mabi=$(ABI) \
 	     -mcmodel=$(CMODEL)
 
 PLATFORM_CPPFLAGS	+= $(ARCH_FLAGS)
